  "result": "I stopped after one gate run, which returned **`WITNESS_FAIL`**. The fault is in the node, not in the two files, so I've reported it in `task_result.md`.\n\n**What fails:** the `branch_1` witness (an electric scooter going clockwise in the roundabout) is planned as `not_applicable`, but the gate returns `unknown` (`aggregate_unresolved:DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`). The node's justification for spans a2/a4 and its narrative say scooters are *excluded* from the vehicle definition. But this run's reading lists `ru.electric_scooter` as *unresolved*, and under the `ru.aggregate` contract an unresolved class makes membership unknown. No scene that matches the narrative can give `not_applicable`. Making the scooter stop to get that verdict would contradict the narrative and leave the exclusion untested.\n\n**The plan needs one of two changes:**\n- **Fix the reading:** classify `ru.electric_scooter` as excluded under `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`, which matches the definition's own words \"excluding … electric scooters\". Then `branch_1` passes with no change to either file.\n- **Fix the scenario:** re-plan `branch_1` to expect `unknown`, or drop it.\n\n**What's written:**\n- **Rule:**\n  - The subject must belong to the vehicle aggregate.\n  - It applies when the subject is in some roundabout and is not stopped.\n  - The obligation: for every roundabout the subject is in, it must not be circulating clockwise. It uses the two node parameters, and I added no narrowings of my own.\n- **Witnesses:** the gate failed only `branch_1`, so `forbid`, `permit`, `idle` and `blind` were not flagged. The car is 20 m east of the roundabout's centre at 10 m/s.\n  - `forbid`: heading south (clockwise).\n  - `permit`: heading north (counterclockwise).\n  - `idle`: a straight street with no roundabout.\n  - `blind`: the roundabout's geometry is hidden.\n\nOne extra shell command I issued by mistake, an empty `python -` call, was blocked automatically because this session can't approve commands. It never ran and didn't count against the gate budget.\n\nFiles are in `.../iter-002/code/LVMC_11_43_010_A/`:\n- task_result.md",
